WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.996 --> 00:00:11.331
&gt;&gt;&gt; A Pennsylvania congressman

00:00:11.465 --> 00:00:12.833
who tried to help Donald Trump

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.036
overturn the 2020 election.

00:00:16.169 --> 00:00:17.204
Republican Scott Perry has been

00:00:17.204 --> 00:00:18.638
fighting to keep his cell phone

00:00:18.772 --> 00:00:20.307
data from D.O.J. Investigators

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:21.808
since it was confiscated by the

00:00:21.942 --> 00:00:22.742
FBI last year.

00:00:22.876 --> 00:00:24.511
Court papers released last night

00:00:24.644 --> 00:00:26.413
say the phone data shows Perry

00:00:26.546 --> 00:00:28.215
was, quote, proactive and

00:00:28.348 --> 00:00:30.016
persistent in contacting the

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.284
executive branch after the

00:00:31.418 --> 00:00:32.519
election and that he was in

00:00:32.652 --> 00:00:33.720
regular contact with then

00:00:33.854 --> 00:00:35.856
president trump and his powerful

00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:36.623
supporters, including white

00:00:36.756 --> 00:00:39.960
house chief of staff mark

00:00:40.093 --> 00:00:40.694
meadows.

00:00:40.827 --> 00:00:44.831
Ellie Hoenig joins us from the

00:00:45.232 --> 00:00:47.601
southern district of New York.

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:48.735
"Untouchable, how powerful

00:00:48.869 --> 00:00:51.605
people get away from it, author

00:00:51.738 --> 00:00:52.772
of that book.

00:00:52.906 --> 00:00:57.244
Congressman Perry has been

00:00:57.377 --> 00:00:59.379
embroiled in a legal battle for

00:00:59.513 --> 00:00:59.713
months.

00:00:59.846 --> 00:01:01.248
How damning is this?

00:01:01.248 --> 00:01:03.250
&gt;&gt; Scott Perry tends to fly

00:01:03.316 --> 00:01:06.686
under the radar like Kevin

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:08.188
Mccarthy, like Jim Jordan who

00:01:08.321 --> 00:01:09.356
were part of the effort to

00:01:09.489 --> 00:01:10.223
overturn the election.

00:01:10.357 --> 00:01:12.192
Scott Perry was even more

00:01:12.325 --> 00:01:13.560
integral as this judge found.

00:01:13.693 --> 00:01:15.562
Perry mostly lost his legal

00:01:15.695 --> 00:01:16.363
argument here.

00:01:16.496 --> 00:01:17.330
He was using something called

00:01:17.464 --> 00:01:19.699
the speech or debate clause

00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:20.734
which basically says members of

00:01:20.867 --> 00:01:22.335
congress cannot be subpoenaed,

00:01:22.469 --> 00:01:24.137
but only about their legislative

00:01:24.271 --> 00:01:24.437
work.

00:01:24.571 --> 00:01:26.106
The judge basically said, the

00:01:26.239 --> 00:01:27.474
vast majority of what was in

00:01:27.607 --> 00:01:29.743
Scott Perry's phone does not

00:01:29.876 --> 00:01:31.278
qualify for protection.

00:01:31.311 --> 00:01:32.379
A very small slice does.

00:01:32.512 --> 00:01:33.413
He's going to have that

00:01:33.547 --> 00:01:34.814
information available to

00:01:34.948 --> 00:01:35.282
investigators.

00:01:35.382 --> 00:01:36.449
He's going to have to answer

00:01:36.583 --> 00:01:36.816
questions.

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:38.051
&gt;&gt; Fascinating.

00:01:38.185 --> 00:01:40.120
Let's turn to Georgia because, I

00:01:40.253 --> 00:01:41.688
mean, as you and I have talked

00:01:41.821 --> 00:01:43.390
about so many times, this is the

00:01:43.523 --> 00:01:45.292
case that worries some of the

00:01:45.292 --> 00:01:46.960
trump folks on that team.

00:01:47.294 --> 00:01:50.063
A judge who oversaw the Georgia

00:01:50.197 --> 00:01:51.298
grand jury investigating efforts

00:01:51.298 --> 00:01:53.300
by trump and his allies to

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:56.036
overturn the 2020 election is

00:01:56.169 --> 00:01:59.306
clarifying what jurors can and

00:01:59.439 --> 00:01:59.839
cannot say.

00:01:59.973 --> 00:02:01.908
Not surprisingly, the judge said

00:02:02.042 --> 00:02:03.443
they cannot discuss

00:02:03.577 --> 00:02:04.444
deliberations but they're free

00:02:04.578 --> 00:02:05.645
to talk about the final report.

00:02:05.779 --> 00:02:07.314
This comes after the foreperson,

00:02:07.314 --> 00:02:08.615
and I know you talked about this

00:02:08.748 --> 00:02:09.983
earlier this past week, went on

00:02:10.116 --> 00:02:13.320
this media blitz and said all

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:14.087
sorts of things.

00:02:14.221 --> 00:02:15.722
Let's listen to that and refresh

00:02:15.855 --> 00:02:16.890
our memory on that.

00:02:17.324 --> 00:02:19.326
&gt;&gt; We definitely heard a lot

00:02:19.326 --> 00:02:21.761
about former president trump and

00:02:21.895 --> 00:02:24.965
we definitely discussed him a

00:02:25.332 --> 00:02:28.935
lot in the room and I will say

00:02:29.069 --> 00:02:30.971
that when this list comes out

00:02:31.338 --> 00:02:33.340
there are no major plot twists

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.474
waiting for you.

00:02:34.608 --> 00:02:37.344
&gt;&gt; Now, Eli, I know you're

00:02:37.477 --> 00:02:38.778
wincing over this and lots of

00:02:38.912 --> 00:02:40.347
other folks were uncomfortable

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:41.982
with what this foreperson was

00:02:42.115 --> 00:02:45.352
saying, and that she was out

00:02:45.418 --> 00:02:46.353
there, maybe enjoying it a

00:02:46.486 --> 00:02:46.920
little too much.

00:02:47.354 --> 00:02:48.822
Your sense of it after digesting

00:02:48.955 --> 00:02:50.490
this for a few days.

00:02:50.624 --> 00:02:51.891
And, I mean, what do you make of

00:02:52.025 --> 00:02:53.793
some of trump's attorneys just

00:02:53.927 --> 00:02:56.630
sort of, you know, almost the

00:02:56.763 --> 00:02:59.032
sky is falling acting as though

00:02:59.366 --> 00:03:04.437
this just blows to smitherines

00:03:04.571 --> 00:03:06.072
the whole case?

00:03:06.206 --> 00:03:07.374
Isn't that stretching things as

00:03:07.374 --> 00:03:07.440
well?

00:03:07.574 --> 00:03:09.376
&gt;&gt; I do think that is a stretch.

00:03:09.476 --> 00:03:10.710
It does not destroy the whole

00:03:10.844 --> 00:03:11.378
case.

00:03:11.378 --> 00:03:12.912
It's bad for prosecutors.

00:03:13.046 --> 00:03:15.048
It's an unnecessary headache for

00:03:15.382 --> 00:03:15.448
prosecutors.

00:03:15.582 --> 00:03:17.384
It's going to result in a meegs

00:03:17.384 --> 00:03:21.388
to dismiss if if there's ever an

00:03:21.388 --> 00:03:21.488
indictment.

00:03:21.621 --> 00:03:23.390
Why have to deal with this as

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:23.757
prosecutors.

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:25.392
The judge clarified correctly

00:03:25.492 --> 00:03:27.060
that the flashpoint here is

00:03:27.394 --> 00:03:28.795
whether this grand juror got

00:03:28.928 --> 00:03:30.397
into, quote, deliberations.

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:32.165
The judge actually passed when

00:03:32.299 --> 00:03:33.400
asked do you think she crossed

00:03:33.533 --> 00:03:33.933
that line.

00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:35.702
He said, well, that's not for

00:03:35.835 --> 00:03:36.169
me.

00:03:36.303 --> 00:03:37.404
It's a close call.

00:03:37.404 --> 00:03:39.806
Just in that clip we heard the

00:03:39.939 --> 00:03:41.408
grand juror say we talked about

00:03:41.441 --> 00:03:42.542
him in the grand jury room,

00:03:42.676 --> 00:03:43.710
meaning Donald Trump.

00:03:43.843 --> 00:03:44.978
Well, one could interpret that

00:03:45.412 --> 00:03:46.112
as deliberations.

00:03:46.246 --> 00:03:47.714
What is the grand jury talking

00:03:47.847 --> 00:03:48.014
about?

00:03:48.148 --> 00:03:51.685
She also mentioned certain other

00:03:51.818 --> 00:03:52.485
specific witnesses by name.

00:03:52.619 --> 00:03:54.087
She told us what the grand jury

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:55.488
made of them.

00:03:55.622 --> 00:03:57.557
She said, for example, we found

00:03:57.691 --> 00:03:59.426
Cassidy Hutchinson credible.

00:03:59.426 --> 00:04:01.094
We found mark meadows less

00:04:01.428 --> 00:04:01.461
credible.

00:04:01.594 --> 00:04:02.729
The argument is going to be that

00:04:02.862 --> 00:04:04.397
that crossed the line into

00:04:04.531 --> 00:04:05.799
talking about deliberations.

00:04:05.932 --> 00:04:07.434
That said, Jim, it's important

00:04:07.434 --> 00:04:09.502
to keep in mind, she's part of a

00:04:09.636 --> 00:04:10.503
special grand jury.

00:04:10.637 --> 00:04:14.040
This is not the grand jury that

00:04:14.174 --> 00:04:14.441
can indict.

00:04:14.574 --> 00:04:19.813
They're proceed video --

00:04:19.946 --> 00:04:20.613
providing information.

00:04:20.747 --> 00:04:22.549
&gt;&gt; There would have to be a

00:04:22.682 --> 00:04:23.983
grand jury to decide a case.

00:04:24.117 --> 00:04:25.785
If the former president were

00:04:25.919 --> 00:04:28.421
indicted the jury would decide

00:04:28.555 --> 00:04:30.490
that case, not this jury, that

00:04:30.623 --> 00:04:30.790
jury.

00:04:30.924 --> 00:04:32.692
&gt;&gt;&gt; Buttoning up the box of

00:04:32.826 --> 00:04:33.993
documents that turned up at

00:04:34.127 --> 00:04:34.394
mar-a-lago.

00:04:34.527 --> 00:04:36.596
Your sense of that latest

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:36.996
development?

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.498
The department of justice wants

00:04:38.631 --> 00:04:39.966
to know how these -- how this

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.835
other box just turned up after

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:43.136
these other searches.

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:44.471
&gt;&gt; Yeah, two big questions.

00:04:44.604 --> 00:04:46.272
How did it get away from

00:04:46.406 --> 00:04:47.507
mar-a-lago while the search was

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:48.942
happening and then find its way

00:04:49.075 --> 00:04:49.576
back after.

00:04:49.709 --> 00:04:52.746
The other thing that jumped out

00:04:52.879 --> 00:04:55.949
to me is we know some aide was

00:04:56.082 --> 00:04:56.716
uploading those classified

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:58.118
materials to a computer or

00:04:58.251 --> 00:04:58.451
laptop.

00:04:58.585 --> 00:05:00.353
If I'm a prosecutor, who gave

00:05:00.487 --> 00:05:01.688
the idea to do that?

00:05:01.821 --> 00:05:03.790
Who gave the instruction to do

00:05:03.923 --> 00:05:04.257
that?

00:05:04.391 --> 00:05:04.524
Why?

00:05:04.657 --> 00:05:05.892
What was done with those

00:05:06.025 --> 00:05:06.259
documents?

